   |b|=3: |b|(3/2)^floor(log_2 X) <= X/4 fails exactly for X in [2, 307] (256 values), holds for all X >= 308; with the sharper carry |b|((3/2)^k - 1): holds for X >= 296
   |b|=5: |b|(3/2)^floor(log_2 X) <= X/4 fails exactly for X in [2, 1153] (897 values), holds for all X >= 1154; with the sharper carry |b|((3/2)^k - 1): holds for X >= 1134
   (at X = 2^t the ratio is (3/4)^t |b|, decreasing in t, so the threshold is final: X_0(1) = 21; the 'X^0.585 <= X/4' reading gives X >= 4^(1/0.415) = 28.3.)
